From 8d12fff8ff6a76bfd289d3a020aa9b3f1c87accb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:29:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 86/86] hir: an unnumbered `_` on the template side of a
 generic match is a fuzzy match

palette 0.7.5, `impl DeltaE for Lch<Wp, T>` calling `Lab::from_color_unclamped(self)`,
with among the candidate impls

    impl<Wp, T, _S> FromColorUnclamped<Rgb<_S, T>> for Lab<Wp, T>
    where <_S as RgbStandard>::Space: RgbSpace<WhitePoint = Wp>, ...

    <null> BUG: ASSERT FAIL: src/hir/type.cpp:876:te.index != ~0u: Encountered ivar for `this` - _

Resolve UFCS paths runs before typecheck. It resolves the path as `<Lab<_, _> as _>`
with unnumbered `_` for the elided generics and checks each `FromColorUnclamped` impl
against `Lab<_, _>`. Matching set `Wp = _`. The bound's `WhitePoint = Wp` then
compared the expected `_` (the template side of `match_test_generics_fuzz`) with
the opaque `<<_S as RgbStandard>::Space as RgbSpace>::WhitePoint`, and `cmp_type`
asserted that the template side never holds an unnumbered ivar. A `_` on the other
side was already a fuzzy match.

Treat it the same way: a `_` with no literal class, unnumbered or not, matches
fuzzily (the existing `InferClass::None` arm). Inference ivars are always numbered,
so this only changes calls that asserted before. The assert stays for unnumbered
integer/float-class ivars.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir/type.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hir/type.cpp b/src/hir/type.cpp
index 7b5e6d1e..a58a9450 100644
--- a/src/hir/type.cpp
+++ b/src/hir/type.cpp
@@ -873,7 +873,10 @@ HIR::TrackHrbStack::PopOnDrop HIR::TrackHrbStack::push_hrb(const std::unique_ptr
     {
         const auto& te = *tep;
         // TODO: Restrict this block with a flag so it panics if an ivar is seen when not expected
-        ASSERT_BUG(sp, te.index != ~0u, "Encountered ivar for `this` - " << v);
+        // - An un-numbered `_` here is an unknown type outside of inference, e.g. the elided generics of a path being
+        //   resolved before typecheck (palette 0.7.5 `Lab::from_color_unclamped(..)` checks impl bounds like
+        //   `S::Space: RgbSpace<WhitePoint = Wp>` with `Wp = _`). Like a `_` on the other side, it matches fuzzily.
+        ASSERT_BUG(sp, te.index != ~0u || te.ty_class == ::HIR::InferClass::None, "Encountered ivar for `this` - " << v);
 
         switch(te.ty_class)
         {
